The Org KPI management suite provides centralized data entry and governance. (1) Key Normalization: Uses a utility ('nk') to collapse spaces and trim strings for consistent matching between ownership and value tables. (2) Progress Scoping: Dashboard progress metrics are dynamically scoped to the selected data owner. (3) State Synchronization: The 'OrgKpiEntryCard' utilizes a secondary 'useEffect' to merge 'sub_factors' and 'achieved_value' from the database into the UI state after the initial load. This ensures data from async queries is correctly populated for employee-scoped rows without overwriting active user edits (guarded by 'isDirtyRef'). (4) Save Integrity: The save handler in 'OrgKpiDataEntry.tsx' implements a specialized guard that permits saving 'sub_factors' even if the 'achieved_value' is null, while preventing the clearing of JSON metadata during unrelated updates by using strict undefined checks. (5) Auditing: 'entered' status distinguishes draft data, and propagation requires explicit confirmation. The 'is_org_kpi_audit_employee' function ensures organization-wide visibility for auditors. (6) Atomic Propagation (v2.66.0): The 'propagate_org_kpi_value' RPC uses ROW_COUNT-guarded status advance and returns {propagated_count, skipped_count, skipped[]}; partial-skip rows are audit-logged as 'PROPAGATION_PARTIAL'. (7) Pre-flight Preview (v2.66.1): The 'preview_org_kpi_propagation' read-only RPC + 'PropagationPreviewDialog' show 'will_advance/will_skip' breakdown before the live call. (8) Reviewer Revision Flow (v2.66.2): Reviewers toggle 'Issue is with the source value' inside SendBackDialog on org-level KPIs to call 'request_org_kpi_revision' — reverts OKV to draft, cascades early-stage employees back to kra_set, flags late-stage employees with 'ORG_KPI_REVISION_FLAGGED', notifies all data owners. (9) Two-Trigger KPI Insertion Pipeline (v2.66.3 + v2.66.6): On every kpis INSERT, two flag-gated triggers fire in sequence — (a) BEFORE INSERT 'trg_autoinherit_org_level_on_kpi_insert' (flag 'enable_org_kpi_auto_inherit', default ON) checks for a sibling KPI with the same (category_id, kra_name, kpi_name, review_period, review_year) signature and 'is_org_level=true', and if found mutates NEW.is_org_level=true and inherits org_level_scope, then (b) AFTER INSERT 'trg_autopull_propagated_org_kpi' (flag 'enable_org_kpi_autopull', activated v2.66.5) finds the most-specific matching propagated/approved OKV (employee → department → org-wide) and pre-fills review_submissions, computes self-score, advances status to self_review. Audit logs: ORG_KPI_AUTO_INHERITED (BEFORE side, via companion AFTER trigger 'trg_audit_org_level_inheritance'), ORG_KPI_AUTOPULLED_FOR_LATE_JOINER (AFTER side). Net effect: a brand-new mid-month KPI matching an existing Org signature instantly becomes Org-level AND gets the achieved value pre-filled if propagated. Both flags toggleable from System Settings → General via 'OrgKpiGovernanceSettings'. (10) Scope Change Cascade + OKV Migration (v2.66.5): 'useChangeOrgKpiScope' calls RPC 'change_org_kpi_scope_cascading' via 'OrgKpiScopeChangeDialog' which offers 'current_only' or 'current_and_future' (cascades to all unlocked open periods in the same fiscal year July→June; locked periods skipped). Helper 'migrate_okv_on_scope_change' handles the 6-way matrix: aggregating transitions (employee/department → broader) AVG-collapse values and inherit highest status (approved > propagated > draft); splitting transitions (broader → narrower) seed 'draft' OKVs for each target owner. Originals archived in 'okv_migration_history' (admin-only RLS) for revert. Audit action: 'ORG_KPI_SCOPE_CASCADED'. (11) Inheritance Reconciler (v2.66.6): RPC 'reconcile_org_kpi_inheritance(p_dry_run)' (admin-only, UI in Data Repair tab as 'OrgKpiInheritanceReconciler') bulk-promotes pre-existing KPIs that should already have inherited Org-level status but didn't (created before the trigger or while the flag was off). Audit action: 'ORG_KPI_INHERITANCE_RECONCILED'.
